ted history is unavailable. Application observes ordered committed entries and independently installs configurations.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-proposal\",\n        \"B-ready\",\n        \"B-config\",\n        \"B-retry\",\n        \"B-application\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-applied\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"S-formation\",\n        \"S-ack\",\n        \"S-log\",\n        \"S-termcommit\",\n        \"S-quorum\",\n        \"S-ready\",\n        \"S-node-loop\",\n        \"S-raw-contract\",\n        \"S-tally\",\n        \"S-changer\",\n        \"S-replication-retry\",\n        \"S-node-advance-contract\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"context\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"Campaign and term handling acquire or lose leader authority. Real candidacy increments term; reset discards peer support and readOnly tracking. A new leader retains history, appends an empty current-term entry and conservatively delays configuration proposals until prior history is applied. Campaign admission scans for unapplied committed configuration entries and requires voter eligibility with no pending snapshot. A pre-vote victory starts a real campaign, and a vote victory becomes leader. Lease/check-quorum policy can suppress disruption; transfer catches up a voter before TimeoutNow, with timed abort. Old-term network replies are filtered before role dispatch; same-term leader traffic makes candidates followers. Restart reconstructs configuration/history and starts follower.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-context\",\n        \"B-recovery\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-applied\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"S-reset\",\n        \"S-election\",\n        \"S-terms\",\n        \"S-hup\",\n        \"S-candidate-votes\",\n        \"S-campaign\",\n        \"S-tally\",\n        \"S-transfer\",\n        \"S-heartbeat-tick\",\n        \"S-init\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"connection\": {\n      \"explanation\": \