{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/skills/evidence-review/guide.md | head -45; nl -ba ../agent-source/rawnode.go | sed -n '65,109p'; nl -ba ../agent-source/node.go | sed -n '265,315p;465,505p;575,605p'; /usr/bin/python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\ns=json.load(open('../submission.schema.json'))['\"'$defs'\"'];print(json.dumps(s['ExploreSubmission'],indent=2))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/skills/evidence-review/guide.md | head -45; nl -ba ../agent-source/rawnode.go | sed -n '65,109p'; nl -ba ../agent-source/node.go | sed -n '265,315p;465,505p;575,605p'; /usr/bin/python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\ns=json.load(open('../submission.schema.json'))['\"'$defs'\"'];print(json.dumps(s['ExploreSubmission'],indent=2))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"SEMANTIC REVIEW Use the supplied contract against fixed inputs, source dependencies and observations. One checker_correspondence review covers requirement versus encoded predicate, entry/caller duties, oracle, identity, legal history, observation path/completion and counterevidence. Use experiments.md for these criteria, including wait/cleanup ownership and finite progress observations; unexamined continuation triggers remain gaps under the stated scheduling assumptions. Applicability and decomposition need separate answers only for concrete issues. No issue found is provisional, not proof or an independent vote.\n\nCURRENT VERSION Cite unchanged established parts and focus on the increment: what changed, which premise it answers, what the new execution observed and what remains unanswered. Verify that the fixed entry, prefix and schedule still exercise the original discriminator: stronger setup must not exclude the investigated premise. A narrower scope cannot settle its parent; substantive changes use the existing revision rules. New inputs require fresh execution and correspondence; old review success cannot certify them. Scope/cause/consequence questions outside the checked proposition are independent limits, not additional confirmation gates. Never alter a requirement or weaken a predicate merely to obtain a passing test.\n\nISSUES Fixed Claim, Harness and Monitor conflicts have exact issue/condition records. Address the listed issue with a sourced resolution and, where supplied, condition dispositions; do not answer the same conflict separately in several products. A no_issue_found item alone clears nothing. Preserve current counterevidence as an open issue, explained alternatives in rationale and independent limits in limitations. Resolution applies to its answering version and descendants; it does not legalize an older driver. Shared semantic issues follow actual dependencies, not checker names.\n\nREPAIR Distinguish review aspect from challenged component. F4 repairs unreached experiment prerequisites. Ordinary technical repair preserves shared property descriptions, events, identities, predicates and legality; it needs no preliminary review or encoding refactor unless an actual dispute/change requires one. Tool, parser and framework failures are not semantic feedback. Executed harness changes require a new artifact, fresh execution and current correspondence. Driver/configuration/initialization repairs name repair_issue_ids, preserve the requirement and oracle, and replace only sourced current premises. Changed observation/oracle encoding uses explicit correction; changed normative meaning/applicability uses F2, and proposition-preserving dependency expansion uses F3. Resolve against the actual changed component, never an unrelated edit. If additional source evidence answers the issue without changing inputs, resolve on that executed version instead of manufacturing a harness rewrite. Remaining issues and the current version's missing correspondence stay visible independently.\n    65\t\trn.raft.tick()\n    66\t}\n    67\t\n    68\t// TickQuiesced advances the internal logical clock by a single tick without\n    69\t// performing any other state machine processing. It allows the caller to avoid\n    70\t// periodic heartbeats and elections when all of the peers in a Raft group are\n    71\t// known to be at the same state. Expected usage is to periodically invoke Tick\n    72\t// or TickQuiesced depending on whether the group is \"active\" or \"quiesced\".\n    73\t//\n    74\t// WARNING: Be very careful about using this method as it subverts the Raft\n    75\t// state machine. You should probably be using Tick instead.\n    76\t//\n    77\t// DEPRECATED: This method will be removed in a future release.\n    78\tfunc (rn *RawNode) TickQuiesced() {\n    79\t\trn.raft.electionElapsed++\n    80\t}\n    81\t\n    82\t// Campaign causes this RawNode to transition to candidate state.\n    83\tfunc (rn *RawNode) Campaign() error {\n    84\t\treturn rn.raft.Step(pb.Message{\n    85\t\t\tType: pb.MsgHup,\n    86\t\t})\n    87\t}\n    88\t\n    89\t// Propose proposes data be appended to the raft log.\n    90\tfunc (rn *RawNode) Propose(data []byte) error {\n    91\t\treturn rn.raft.Step(pb.Message{\n    92\t\t\tType: pb.MsgProp,\n    93\t\t\tFrom: rn.raft.id,\n    94\t\t\tEntries: []pb.Entry{\n    95\t\t\t\t{Data: data},\n    96\t\t\t}})\n    97\t}\n    98\t\n    99\t// ProposeConfChange proposes a config change. See (Node).ProposeConfChange for\n   100\t// details.\n   101\tfunc (rn *RawNode) ProposeConfChange(cc pb.ConfChangeI) error {\n   102\t\tm, err := confChangeToMsg(cc)\n   103\t\tif err != nil {\n   104\t\t\treturn err\n   105\t\t}\n   106\t\treturn rn.raft.Step(m)\n   107\t}\n   108\t\n   109\t// ApplyConfChange applies a config change to the local node. The app must call\n   265\t\t\tc.Logger.Warningf(\"error occurred during starting a new node: %v\", err)\n   266\t\t}\n   267\t\n   268\t\tn := newNode(rn)\n   269\t\treturn &n\n   270\t}\n   271\t\n   272\t// StartNode returns a new Node given configuration and a list of raft peers.\n   273\t// It appends a ConfChangeAddNode entry for each given peer to the initial log.\n   274\t//\n   275\t// Peers must not be zero length; call RestartNode in that case.\n   276\tfunc StartNode(c *Config, peers []Peer) Node {\n   277\t\tn := setupNode(c, peers)\n   278\t\tgo n.run()\n   279\t\treturn n\n   280\t}\n   281\t\n   282\t// RestartNode is similar to StartNode but does not take a list of peers.\n   283\t// The current membership of the cluster will be restored from the Storage.\n   284\t// If the caller has an existing state machine, pass in the last log index that\n   285\t// has been applied to it; otherwise use zero.\n   286\tfunc RestartNode(c *Config) Node {\n   287\t\trn, err := NewRawNode(c)\n   288\t\tif err != nil {\n   289\t\t\tpanic(err)\n   290\t\t}\n   291\t\tn := newNode(rn)\n   292\t\tgo n.run()\n   293\t\treturn &n\n   294\t}\n   295\t\n   296\ttype msgWithResult struct {\n   297\t\tm      pb.Message\n   298\t\tresult chan error\n   299\t}\n   300\t\n   301\t// node is the canonical implementation of the Node interface\n   302\ttype node struct {\n   303\t\tpropc      chan msgWithResult\n   304\t\trecvc      chan pb.Message\n   305\t\tconfc      chan pb.ConfChangeV2\n   306\t\tconfstatec chan pb.ConfState\n   307\t\treadyc     chan Ready\n   308\t\tadvancec   chan struct{}\n   309\t\ttickc      chan struct{}\n   310\t\tdone       chan struct{}\n   311\t\tstop       chan struct{}\n   312\t\tstatus     chan chan Status\n   313\t\n   314\t\trn *RawNode\n   315\t}\n   465\t\tcase n.tickc <- struct{}{}:\n   466\t\tcase <-n.done:\n   467\t\tdefault:\n   468\t\t\tn.rn.raft.logger.Warningf(\"%x A tick missed to fire. Node blocks too long!\", n.rn.raft.id)\n   469\t\t}\n   470\t}\n   471\t\n   472\tfunc (n *node) Campaign(ctx context.Context) error { return n.step(ctx, pb.Message{Type: pb.MsgHup}) }\n   473\t\n   474\tfunc (n *node) Propose(ctx context.Context, data []byte) error {\n   475\t\treturn n.stepWait(ctx, pb.Message{Type: pb.MsgProp, Entries: []pb.Entry{{Data: data}}})\n   476\t}\n   477\t\n   478\tfunc (n *node) Step(ctx context.Context, m pb.Message) error {\n   479\t\t// Ignore unexpected local messages receiving over network.\n   480\t\tif IsLocalMsg(m.Type) && !IsLocalMsgTarget(m.From) {\n   481\t\t\t// TODO: return an error?\n   482\t\t\treturn nil\n   483\t\t}\n   484\t\treturn n.step(ctx, m)\n   485\t}\n   486\t\n   487\tfunc confChangeToMsg(c pb.ConfChangeI) (pb.Message, error) {\n   488\t\ttyp, data, err := pb.MarshalConfChange(c)\n   489\t\tif err != nil {\n   490\t\t\treturn pb.Message{}, err\n   491\t\t}\n   492\t\treturn pb.Message{Type: pb.MsgProp, Entries: []pb.Entry{{Type: typ, Data: data}}}, nil\n   493\t}\n   494\t\n   495\tfunc (n *node) ProposeConfChange(ctx context.Context, cc pb.ConfChangeI) error {\n   496\t\tmsg, err := confChangeToMsg(cc)\n   497\t\tif err != nil {\n   498\t\t\treturn err\n   499\t\t}\n   500\t\treturn n.Step(ctx, msg)\n   501\t}\n   502\t\n   503\tfunc (n *node) step(ctx context.Context, m pb.Message) error {\n   504\t\treturn n.stepWithWaitOption(ctx, m, false)\n   505\t}\n   575\t\tc := make(chan Status)\n   576\t\tselect {\n   577\t\tcase n.status <- c:\n   578\t\t\treturn <-c\n   579\t\tcase <-n.done:\n   580\t\t\treturn Status{}\n   581\t\t}\n   582\t}\n   583\t\n   584\tfunc (n *node) ReportUnreachable(id uint64) {\n   585\t\tselect {\n   586\t\tcase n.recvc <- pb.Message{Type: pb.MsgUnreachable, From: id}:\n   587\t\tcase <-n.done:\n   588\t\t}\n   589\t}\n   590\t\n   591\tfunc (n *node) ReportSnapshot(id uint64, status SnapshotStatus) {\n   592\t\trej := status == SnapshotFailure\n   593\t\n   594\t\tselect {\n   595\t\tcase n.recvc <- pb.Message{Type: pb.MsgSnapStatus, From: id, Reject: rej}:\n   596\t\tcase <-n.done:\n   597\t\t}\n   598\t}\n   599\t\n   600\tfunc (n *node) TransferLeadership(ctx context.Context, lead, transferee uint64) {\n   601\t\tselect {\n   602\t\t// manually set 'from' and 'to', so that leader can voluntarily transfers its leadership\n   603\t\tcase n.recvc <- pb.Message{Type: pb.MsgTransferLeader, From: transferee, To: lead}:\n   604\t\tcase <-n.done:\n   605\t\tcase <-ctx.Done():\n{\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"rationale\": {\n      \"minLength\": 1,\n      \"title\": \"Rationale\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"sources\": {\n      \"default\": [],\n      \"items\": {\n        \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/SourceRange\"\n      },\n      \"title\": \"Sources\",\n      \"type\": \"array\"\n    },\n    \"feedback\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/ResearchFeedback\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"default\": null\n    },\n    \"repair_of\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"default\": null,\n      \"description\": \"Rejected operation ID whose complete draft this submission repairs\",\n      \"title\": \"Repair Of\"\n    },\n    \"action\": {\n      \"const\": \"explore\",\n      \"title\": \"Action\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"question\": {\n      \"minLength\": 1,\n      \"title\": \"Question\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"harness_path\": {\n      \"title\": \"Harness Path\",\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"execution_package\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"null\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"default\": null,\n      \"description\": \"Optional single local Go package or Rust crate directory, with the same meaning as Harness.execution_package\",\n      \"title\": \"Execution Package\"\n    },\n    \"files\": {\n      \"additionalProperties\": {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n      },\n      \"default\": {},\n      \"title\": \"Files\",\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"rationale\",\n    \"action\",\n    \"question\",\n    \"harness_path\"\n  ],\n  \"title\": \"ExploreSubmission\",\n  \"type\": \"object\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
